  "problem": "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14004554/assets/a8264c635006c74c2d9a7ca4eb3ab8d937ae7b270b4567373d022186c787bbc1.png)\n\nAn artist makes a glass sculpture. In the figure, the areas of some of the faces are displayed in a net of the sculpture. What is the total surface area of the sculpture?",
  "worked_solution": "The net shown corresponds to a triangular prism. The surface area of our prism consists of $2$ triangles (base and top) and $3$ rectangles (central and side faces). \n\nTherefore, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Surface area} & =2\\times (\\text{Area of the base})+3\\times (\\text{Area of the side faces}) \\\\  & =2\\times 8+3\\times 17 \\\\  & =16+51 \\\\  & =67\\,{\\text{m}}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
